  "details": "I uploaded sample Excellent robot avatars with 31 & 41 face tracking Forwarded Parameters to force the avatars down to Poor & Very Poor rank. The client reports the avatar's performance rating as both Excellent and Poor/Very Poor, which is incorrect.\n\nAffected private avatars by WubTheCaptain:\n\n- Robot （Poor forwarded parameters） `avtr_f65a0f15-6f36-400a-a7bd-42f5dbcbf78a`\n\n- Robot （Very Poor forwarded parameters） `avtr_f65a0f15-6f36-400a-a7bd-42f5dbcbf78a`\n\nExpected result: Poor (31 forwarded parameters) or Very Poor (41 forwarded parameters), as reported in the SDK (`3.10.6`) and in performance stats of the avatar (VRChat 2026.4.1p3 Build `1939`).\n\nActual result:\n\n- The client reports the avatars as Excellent in \"My Avatars\" icon. (incorrect)\n\n- The client displays both \"Excellent\" and \"Poor\"/\"Very Poor\" text with performance ratings in avatar details. (incorrect)\n\n- Poor or Very Poor are displayed on the nameplate. (correct)\n\n- Local SDK test avatar build reports the avatars as \"Poor\" or \"Very Poor\". (correct)",
